  "num_turns": null,
  "final_message": "I fixed the bug in `add_tag`, and the public test now passes (`python3 -m unittest -v test_public.py`: 1 test, OK).\n\n**The bug:** `add_tag(record, tag, tags=[])` used a list as its default value. Python creates that list only once and reuses it on every call, so tags added in one call showed up in later, unrelated calls.\n\n**The fix:** the default is now `tags=None`, and the function creates a new empty list whenever `tags` isn't passed. If the caller passes a list, `add_tag` still appends to that same list rather than a copy. I checked this: the caller's list becomes `['x', 'y']`. `remove_tag` is unchanged.\n\nDONE: Fixed add_tag's shared-list default by using tags=None and creating a fresh list per call; caller-supplied lists are still modified in place.",
